@Haroenv it seems to work on some points.

When I then go to an object and go back i get this error: 
![image](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/65391517/138721996-6b54467c-0f56-4e2d-834e-f8e437161469.png)

I assume this is because it writes after the router is disposed, you can override this by using:

```js
router: {...historyRouter(), dispose() {

      if (typeof window === 'object' && this._onPopState) {
        window.removeEventListener('popstate', this._onPopState);
      }


    if (this.writeTimer) {
      clearTimeout(this.writeTimer);
    }
} },
```

Thanks @Haroenv 
If I have the routing object like this: 
```
routing: {
			router: {
				...historyRouter(), 
				dispose() {
					if (typeof window === 'object' && this._onPopState) {
						window.removeEventListener('popstate', this._onPopState);
					}
					if (this.writeTimer) {
						clearTimeout(this.writeTimer);
					}
				} 
			},
		}
```

it gives me this error: 
